  "notes": "Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (Total column, p4). Beginning fund balance is 'as previously reported' 35,513,681 with the 54,646 restatement as an adjustment (as restated = 35,568,327). Debt proceeds = bonds issued 34,020,000 + SBITA issuance 150,348 (computed); other_financing = premium on debt issued 1,038,153; transfers in (out), net 268,000 recorded as transfers_in. SBITA interest printed as dash, omitted. ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet total cash (p3). Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1). Business-type = Waste Water Fund (p8): no single printed receipts/disbursements totals, so reported_totals are computed sums (receipts 13,862,653+34,480+236,116; disbursements = operating expenses 11,948,511 + interest expense 29,855, which equals Waste water expenses on p2). Transfers out 268,000 as transfers_net. Business-type net position rolls forward: 26,011,850 + 14,133,249 - 11,978,366 - 268,000 = 27,898,733. The report has no budget schedule for the Waste Water (business-type) fund, so there are no business-type budget-schedule detail lines; its lines are in receipts/disbursements from the proprietary statement p8. Detail schedules (General, Community Betterment, LB840) are budget-basis and differ from GAAP statement amounts; they show function only, so expenditure detail_category is 'not itemized'. Community Betterment transfers out shown as negative. LB840 schedule has no budget column. Re-extracted from scratch with every page re-read. Read pages 1-10 of 10 Detail rebuilt 2026-10-27 from the governmental funds statement fund columns (user: statement, not budget schedules). Budget-basis schedules (General p5, Community Betterment p6) and the LB840 schedule (p10) removed. No nonmajor combining statement in the trimmed PDF, so the statement Other Governmental Funds column is used.",
  "decision_needed": [
